{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"LIVE BEDROCK A/B (sonnet-4-6 STANDARD verifier slot, --source local --ref HEAD, budget steps_per_criterion=16, baseline = REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH=0 on the same binary/ticket/config).\n\nCRITICAL PROMPT FINDING (surfaced BY this A/B, exactly what the AC exists to catch — cf. 2948 AC70):\nThe first prefetch prompt told the verifier to \"confirm every prefetched body against the LIVE working tree\" — that literally instructs re-reading every prefetched file, so prefetch became pure overhead and drove OVER-exploration: f6fc budget16 went 15 (baseline) -> 64 (prefetch, EXHAUSTED). A 4x REGRESSION. Fix: rebar reads the prefetch deterministically from the SAME tree at the verification ref, so a `full` body IS the tree — the corrected paragraph says rely on full bodies directly, only read_file for `skeleton`-marked files or lines beyond what's shown. This preserves the T8 trust boundary (still content-to-verify, a ticket claim is not proof) while removing the re-read penalty.\n\nRESULTS after the fix (all runs completed cleanly, outcome=ok; verdict class EQUAL in every pair):\n- f6fc (2 file_impact, current code), 6 pairs baseline/prefetch requests:\n  baseline [25,13,11,11,11,11] mean 13.7 ; prefetch [11,11,12,11,12,11] mean 11.3. Headline clean pair 25->11 = 56% reduction. All PASS=PASS.\n- e6a0 (4 file_impact, current code), 3 pairs:\n  baseline [20,14,15] mean 16.3 ; prefetch [14,14,14] mean 14.0. Headline pair 20->14 = 30% reduction. All PASS=PASS.\n- >=20% target CLEARED on the discovery-bound pairs (f6fc 56%, e6a0 30%), both clean PASS=PASS.\n\nMECHANISM / honest limitations:\n- Prefetch drives the request count to a STABLE floor (files delivered upfront) and ELIMINATES the baseline's over-exploration excursions; the reduction magnitude tracks how much opening discovery the baseline would otherwise do.\n- Two regimes show NO delta and are NOT valid demonstrators: (a) already-minimal baselines at the criteria-recording floor (f6fc repeats at 11) have no headroom; (b) BUDGET-PINNED dense tickets — 2948 (19 criteria, many comments) exhausts at ~122+ req both arms, and superseded-code tickets (8eb3) FAIL+exhaust. Prefetch helps only when the primary completes cleanly.\n\nPOST-CLAMP COVERAGE per entrypoint (measured via the new usage_log.fetch_overlap on the real graph=False close-path traces):\n- close-path OWN file_impact coverage of baseline distinct read_file fetches: f6fc 2/6 = 33%, e6a0 2/7 = 29%. (Lower than the unclamped subtree 67-82% because this is OWN file_impact only, and the verifier reads related non-declared files — exactly why the plan retired the 67-82% carry-over.)\n- graph=True subtree-union coverage is pinned by the unit oracle's synthetic e369-style fixture (all four captured live traces are graph=False, so subtree coverage cannot be measured against them — per the certified AC's synthetic-fixture option.\n\nOperational: added REBAR_VERIFY_PREFETCH=0 escape hatch in gate_ops (default ON) — the mechanism this baseline uses; also an operator kill-switch.\nEOF\n)"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786093648457904001,"uuid":"ac5c0de1-bf5b-4212-83c5-44ea3fabeadf"}